        "timestamp": 1778255637,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. UK: The end of the traditional two-party system? Starmer faces crushing defeat in local polls Europe Issued on: 08/05/2026 - 17:53 Early results from the UK local elections point to a crushing defeat for Starmer’s Labour Party. The hard-right Reform UK looked set to pick up some 400 seats, stealing hundreds from both the Conservative Party and Labour. The Greens and the Liberal Democrats, meanwhile, recorded relatively modest but significant gains. According to analysts, this could mark the end of the traditional British two-party system, with voters shifting to the two extremes of the political spectrum. Story by Eliza Herbert. Substantial win for Nigel Farage's Reform UK in local elections 08/05/2026 Europe Energy security vs climate crisis: Norway reopens three old gas fields 08/05/2026 Europe Keir Starmer's Labour braces for heavy losses in UK local elections 08/05/2026 Europe Russia and Ukraine trade major attacks despite Victory Day ceasefire 08/05/2026 Europe 'Ici c'est Paris': Defending champions PSG 'on the verge of making history' 07/05/2026 Sport 3 patients are being evacuated to Europe from ship with hantavirus outbreak 06/05/2026 Europe War in Ukraine: Russia attacks east and south Ukraine with over 100 drones 06/05/2026 Europe Hantavirus-hit cruise ship heads to Spain to dock in Canary Islands 06/05/2026 Europe Kyiv says Russia broke unilateral ceasefire with drone and missile attacks 06/05/2026 Europe"
