        "orario": "17:28",
        "timestamp": 1778254080,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Middle East war back on? UAE responds to fresh attacks, US and Iran trade fire Middle East Issued on: 08/05/2026 - 17:28 The United Arab Emirates says it's responded to fresh missile and drone attacks by Iran this Friday. The strikes come hours after the US says three of its navy destroyers in the Strait of Hormuz were targeted. President Donald Trump ordered retaliatory strikes - but then downplayed the hostilities and said the ceasefire still stands. Analysis by Douglas Herbert, FRANCE 24 international affairs commentator. Iran and the US trade fire over Hormuz, Trump says ceasefire still in effect 08/05/2026 Middle East Israel and Hezbollah continue to trade blows despite the ceasefire 08/05/2026 Middle East Iran on the verge of economic asphyxiation -- rare footage from Tehran 08/05/2026 Middle East What we know about the latest exchange of fire between the US and Iran 08/05/2026 Middle East China's 'key priorities': Open Hormuz, get oil flowing, avoid 'getting dragged into conflicts' 06/05/2026 Asia / Pacific 'Significant threat to local ecosystem: Israel's war on Lebanon generated 16 million tons of rubble' 06/05/2026 Middle East Iran Nobel winner Narges Mohammadi at risk of dying in custody 06/05/2026 Middle East US suspends Hormuz operation: Washington believes close to deal with Iran 06/05/2026 Middle East Iran Nobel Peace Prize winner Narges Mohammadi 'between life and death' 06/05/2026 Middle East"
